      "writtenOn": "2026-07-09T12:33:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This custom method makes it hard for the user to reason about when using this class. More specifically, ThreadPoolExecutor exposes a method with the same name which returns a different value, and if someone is familiar with that framework class, they would expect this method to do the same thing. When considering the Java classes, I believe getMaxPoolSize() is more representative of what this method does? Can we improve this class so that it does not expose any methods with custom meanings by either extending an existing framework class, or implementing an existing framework interface? \n\nThere are several new classes is this change with names such as Executor which imply they are classes from the framework classes, and they are not. I would advise either remaining them to avoid confusion, or bringing them more inline with the contracts of the framework classes.",
